theory.intro:
To estimate $f'(c)$ from a graph, draw the **tangent** touching the curve at that point. Pick two clear grid points on the tangent and find its gradient, $m = \dfrac{\text{rise}}{\text{run}}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[gray!30,very thin] (0,0) grid (5,5);
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (5.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0.2:4.0,smooth,variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.25*\x*\x + 1}) node[above left] {$y=f(x)$};
\draw[thick,red] (0.6,0.6) -- (4.6,4.6) node[right,font=\small] {tangent};
\draw[dashed,gray] (1,1) -- (4,1) node[midway,below,font=\small] {run};
\draw[dashed,gray] (4,1) -- (4,4) node[midway,right,font=\small] {rise};
\fill (1,1) circle (2.5pt) node[below right,font=\small] {$(x_1,y_1)$};
\fill (4,4) circle (2.5pt) node[below right,font=\small] {$(x_2,y_2)$};
\fill (2,2) circle (2.5pt) node[below right,font=\small] {$P$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
The graph of $y = f(x)$ has a tangent line drawn at $(2, 4)$ passing through $(0, 0)$ and $(4, 8)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (5.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8,5/10} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:4.4,smooth,variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.25*\x*\x + 1}) node[above left] {$y=f(x)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0,0) -- (4.5,4.5);
\fill (2,2.0) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above left,font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (2,2.0) {$(2,4)$};
\fill (4,4.0) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below right,font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (4,4.0) {$(4,8)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Estimate the instantaneous rate of change $f'(2)$.

The graph shows the temperature $T$ ($^{\circ}\text{C}$) of a cooling object over $t$ minutes, with a tangent drawn at $t = 10\text{ min}$ passing through $(0, 70)$ and $(30, 10)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (6.5,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$T$};
\foreach \x/\val in {1/10,2/20,3/30,4/40,5/50,6/60} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\val$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/20,2/40,3/60,4/80,5/100} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:6,smooth,variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.5 + 3.297*exp(-0.5*\x)}) node[above right] {$T(t)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0,3.5) -- (3.5,0.0);
\fill (1,2.5) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above right,font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (1,2.5) {$(10,50)$};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.3,2.75) {Temperature ($^{\circ}\text{C}$)};
\node[below] at (3.2,-0.9) {Time (min)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Estimate the instantaneous rate of cooling at $t = 10\text{ minutes}$.

The graph shows a curve with tangents drawn at $x = 1$ and at $x = 4$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (5.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8,5/10} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0.5:4.6,smooth,variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.125*\x*\x + 0.375}) node[above left] {$y=f(x)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0.2,0.3) -- (2.5,0.875) node[right] {$T_1$};
\draw[thick,dashed,teal] (2.8,1.175) -- (4.8,3.175) node[right] {$T_2$};
\fill (1,0.5) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (4,2.375) circle (2.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Compare the instantaneous rate of change at $x = 1$ with that at $x = 4$.

The graph of $y = f(x)$ shows a tangent line drawn at $(1, 1)$ passing through $(0, -1)$ and $(2, 3)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (-1,0) -- (4.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2) -- (0,4.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {-1,1,2,3,4} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue] plot[smooth,tension=0.6] coordinates {(-0.5,0.25) (0,0) (1,1) (2,4)} node[above left] {$y=f(x)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (-0.5,-2) -- (2.5,4);
\fill (1,1) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$(1,1)$};
\fill (0,-1) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$(0,-1)$};
\fill (2,3) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$(2,3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Calculate the estimated value of $f'(1)$.

The distance–time graph of an accelerating vehicle shows a tangent drawn at $t = 4\text{ s}$ passing through $(2, 10)$ and $(6, 50)$, where distance is in metres.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (6.5,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$d$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/10,2/20,3/30,4/40,5/50} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:6,smooth] plot (\x, {0.0625*\x*\x + 0.5*\x}) node[above left] {$d(t)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (1,0.0) -- (6,5.0);
\fill (4,3.0) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above left,font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (4,3.0) {$(4,30)$};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.3,2.75) {Distance (m)};
\node[below] at (3.2,-0.9) {Time (s)};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
Estimate the instantaneous speed of the vehicle at $t = 4\text{ seconds}$.

The graph shows $y = f(x)$ with a tangent at $(3, 6)$ passing through $(1, 2)$ and $(5, 10)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (6.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8,5/10} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0.4:4.8,smooth,variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.12*\x*\x + 0.28*\x + 1.08}) node[above left] {$y=f(x)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0.5,0.5) -- (5.3,5.3);
\fill (3,3.0) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$(3,6)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the estimated value of $f'(3)$.

development.question_text:
The graph shows the volume $V$ (mL) of gas produced in a chemical reaction over time $t$ (seconds), with a tangent drawn at $t = 20\text{ s}$ passing through $(0, 15)$ and $(40, 75)$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (6.5,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$V$};
\foreach \x/\val in {1/10,2/20,3/30,4/40,5/50,6/60} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below] at (\x,-0.12) {$\val$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/20,2/40,3/60,4/80,5/100} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:5.5,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x}, {4.227*(1 - exp(-0.38*\x))}) node[above] {$V(t)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0,0.75) -- (5,4.5);
\fill (2,2.25) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$(20,45)$};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.4,2.75) {Volume (mL)};
\node[below] at (3.25,-0.9) {Time (s)};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
Estimate the instantaneous rate of reaction at $t = 20\text{ seconds}$.

The graph of $y = g(x)$ shows a tangent line drawn at $(2, 5)$ passing through $(0, 9)$ and $(4, 1)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (5.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8,5/10} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0.4:4.4,smooth,variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.25*\x*\x - 2*\x + 5.5}) node[above right] {$y=g(x)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0,4.5) -- (4.5,0.0);
\fill (2,2.5) circle (2.5pt) node[above right] {$(2,5)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Estimate the derivative value $g'(2)$.

The graph of $y = f(x)$ shows a tangent line drawn at $(0, 2)$ passing through $(-2, -4)$ and $(2, 8)$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (-3,0) -- (3.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.5) -- (0,4.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-2,-1,1,2,3} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {-2/-4,-1/-2,1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=-1.9:2.3,smooth] plot (\x, {-0.15*\x*\x + 1.5*\x + 1.0}) node[above left] {$y=f(x)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (-2,-2) -- (2,4);
\fill (0,1.0) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$(0,2)$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
Find the value of $f'(0)$.

mastery.question_text:
The graph of $y = f(x)$ shows a polynomial with a local maximum at $x = -2$ and a local minimum at $x = 3$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (-3.5,0) -- (4.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.5) -- (0,3.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue] plot[smooth,tension=0.6] coordinates {(-3.2,0.8) (-2,2.5) (-0.5,1.2) (1,0) (3,-1.8) (4,0.5)} node[above left] {$y=f(x)$};
\fill (-2,2.5) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (3,-1.8) circle (2.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
State the exact value of $f'(-2)$ and $f'(3)$, and state the sign of $f'(0)$.
